    "intro_html":  "Maqluba means upside down in Arabic, and the traditional finish is a piece of theater: the whole pot gets flipped onto a platter at the table and everyone holds their breath. For meal prep we skip the drama and scoop it out, which changes nothing about the taste. What matters is the layering, chicken on the bottom, then vegetables, then rice, all cooking in one pot with allspice and cinnamon running through it. Each bowl comes in at \u003cstrong\u003e574 calories and 33 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$1.37\u003c/strong\u003e.",
